  "content_en": "10. Little Woman Troubles - fair and wealthy, harmonious, respecting mother-in-law above all, caring for sisters-in-law below, born in a famous family, stable and capable. Mrs. Zou has always been a perfect existence in the Hou family, but the only flaw is that such a daughter-in-law does not seem to win the heart of her mother-in-law! \"The eldest daughter-in-law is here, come and sit down. I wonder how the fifth aunt is doing? Is the child okay?\" But it seems different today. The old lady showed obvious enthusiasm for Zou's arrival. Maybe it was the drama of infighting and secret fighting that just happened here that made the old man feel exhausted. \"Well, thank you, Mrs. Old Lady, for your concern. Everything is fine. This fifth aunt has taken good care of her child since she was pregnant. This minor illness and calamity will naturally not cause anything.\" Zou immediately smiled again. \"Look at me... I only talked about gossip and forgot to say hello to the old lady. I was already late, and now... oh, I really deserve a beating!\" Mrs. Zou continued, making a show of saluting. \"Okay, okay, you are not in love with each other. We ladies, please stop doing those false etiquettes. It's not easy for you either. Come and have a drink of tea!\" The old lady quickly stopped her. The Zou family did not bow again, thanked the old lady again, and then greeted the Miao family and the Jiang family's sisters-in-law. The third sister Wen, the sixth sister Wen, the eighth sister Wen who came over there with the Zou family, and a special being, the seventh sister Wen, also paid their respects to the old lady. Facing a group of beautiful granddaughters, the old lady seemed to be in a better mood. She chatted with them in a pleasant manner. Finally, she smiled and asked the third sister how the embroidery of her trousseau was going. Third Sister Wen is tall and beautiful, with generous manners, but she has a cold temperament. She is usually stern, but at this moment, when her grandmother who loved her teased her, she couldn't help but blush and become shy. Everyone in the room laughed instantly... But in the midst of the excitement, Cuiping suddenly came in in a hurry and whispered something in the ear of the second lady's eldest girl, Cui Xiu. Cuixiu was startled, and then quietly walked to the second lady and whispered to her. The second lady frowned slightly, then stood up, quietly turning around and retreating with Cuixiu. No one noticed that there were two missing people in the room at this moment, but Sister Wenjiu was not included in the crowd. The numerous female relatives of the Wen Mansion, plus the maids and wives, were crowded together. No matter how big the room was, it was already full. She, an insignificant person, was squeezed into the corner of the room, right next to the door curtain. In addition, she is alert and careful, so she naturally took this scene into account. Of course, this is not surprising. There are a lot of aunts and servants in every house, and emergencies can happen at any time. What made her feel strange was that after the second lady's master and servant went out, the eldest lady who was surrounded by everyone suddenly turned her head and smiled at Cuiping, and Cuiping smiled back at her before turning around and going out. Ah... Sister Ninth couldn't help but be slightly startled. But she soon understood - it didn't take long, and the second lady hurried back, but the seat she just sat next to the old lady was already occupied by someone, and that was the eldest lady Zou. The second lady had no choice but to sit on one side and watched eagerly as the old lady and Zou talked and laughed, squeezing the handkerchief tightly with her thin white fingers. Sister Ninth couldn't help but suddenly realized that there must be a reason for Zou's lateness, otherwise how could it be so perfect? In fact, she heard yesterday that the fifth concubine of Uncle Ningping Hou, who was pregnant with a child, was suffering from cold. It was just a minor illness at first, but it continued to cause trouble until this morning, and even alerted the old lady. This must have been deliberately exaggerated by someone. How come such a mistress who attaches so much importance to treating her concubine and her child well is not praised by others? Either sooner or later, if you choose to appear happily and innocently after the struggle and your feelings are hurt, you will naturally be welcomed, so why not please? Sigh... No wonder he had to seize such a huge Marquis Mansion without leakage. It was really a good trick! \"Sister Ninth, let's go!\" At this moment, she heard Sister Ten next to her calling her. She was startled and realized that all the sisters had dispersed and were walking towards the door. Only a few wives were left in the room. She quickly followed behind Sister Ten... It should be time for the male family members to pay their respects, and they were going to Qingya Pavilion for class. Coming out of the Yanshou Hall, along a bluestone-paved corridor, you go straight to the garden. Then you turn a corner and see a small courtyard with blue bricks and white walls. That is the place where they study - Qingya Pavilion. The eldest sister Wen has already left the court, the second sister Wen died young, and the third sister Wen stopped her studies as her wedding day was approaching and concentrated on embroidering the dowry. The fifth sister Wen has been \"sick\" again, so she is sitting in the Qingya Pavilion now.There are only seven girls left. Some people say that three women perform a show, and there are seven sitting here at once. Although they are all still young women, it does not prevent them from causing a few minor disturbances every day, especially when there is a presence like Sister Wen Liu. But when it comes to turmoil, what comes and goes is just those bad dramas - the wild and arrogant Sixth Sister bullies her concubine Sister Wenba, and the weak and crybaby Sister Wenba is bullied by her eldest sister Wen Liu. Then the sixth sister took the seventh sister and got into trouble with the good school formed by the fourth and ten sisters. Of course, the fourth sister and the tenth sister reported the sixth sister to Mr. Yun who only knew how to have fun and misbehave all day long... The eleventh sister because of the fourth lady, no one wanted to get close to her, and because of her young age, almost no one paid attention to her. As for Sister Ninth, besides watching silently, she occasionally talked to Sister Eight and Sister Ten, but she never got involved in any fights. One is that this child's trick is really boring; the other is that he keeps a low profile and hides his clumsiness and does not want to be an enemy. But today's fuss seems a bit too much - \"Sixth sister, do you know that such a fancy spider is poisonous and will cause trouble if it bites someone? Get it away quickly - throw it out!\" \"Really? You even know this. Fourth sister is really knowledgeable, but what if I don't take it away?\" ...It’s unreasonable, I tell you, if you don’t take it away, I will sue you...” “You dare...” “Do you think I dare you?” “Sister Wen, you really go... stop, do you hear me, or... or I’ll let this spider bite you...” Then there was a chaotic sound of running and tearing. \"Ah——\" followed by a scream. \"Eighth sister...\" \"Eighth sister...\" followed by a burst of frightened and nervous shouting. \"Eighth Sister...Eighth Sister was scared to death by that spider...\" Finally, Eleventh Sister concluded tremblingly. ……————————Digression——————Dear friends, Happy New Year! I changed the character list, and the fourth sister, fifth sister, and seventh sister were all changed to thirteen years old!",
